        "notes": "Reason(s) why I chose what I did:\n\n**Power**:\nThe power I chose to always get round one is [Triage Unit](item_fec0554c-2685-4b93-822d-bf0020e654b4).\nThe reason why I chose this is because it really helps keeping your teammates alive especially if you have a duo you're pocketing and don't want them to die. It is important to always try to time your Guardian Angel ability for when a teammate gets below 50% to give them the extra boost of healing. Since Mercy is a pocket hero, giving whoever you're pocketing extra healing when below half hp can help you win team fights when the enemy team does more damage that you normally can't out heal.\n\n**Perks**:\nFor round one I always choose to get  [First Aid Kit](item_0172eaaa-1902-44a3-b989-d12f0f7301da),  [Compensator](item_2a354f80-610c-4661-9bdd-8960ae1a60b0), and  [Weapon Grease](item_961ae72f-434f-406b-a89b-ab8efec806bf).\nThe reason why I choose these perks is because having weapon power and attack speed on mercy increases her healing per second which can make her really valuable since in regular role queue it is well known that Mercy's healing isn't that great. Weapon power and attack speed heal the same amount of hp per second so it doesn't matter if one is higher than the other because they go towards the same thing, faster healing per second. Getting the [First Aid Kit](item_0172eaaa-1902-44a3-b989-d12f0f7301da) also helps keep yourself alive which is very important because with this build you are now the win condition for your team as long as you're alive. You eventually will have healed an average 14k+ heals per 10 minutes while still having a positive damage boost percentage to help enable your team which will get you focused by the enemy team and which is why it is important you stay alive especially.",
